      "publicationDate": "1989-01-01",
      "title": "Kinetic mechanism of the water-gas-shift reaction over K/sub 2/CO/sub 3//carbon",
      "type": "article",
      "url": "https://openalex.org/works/W2299040644",
      "abstract": "Kinetic data of the alkali catalyzed WGS reaction can be described by a two step oxygen-exchange mechanism and an additional CO/sub 2/-chemisorption step. The Water-Gas-Shift reaction rate is dependent on both the partial pressure of the reducing and the oxidizing agent. In the presence of CO/sub 2/ in the gas phase reactivity is low, or decreases significantly if CO/sub 2/ is added to a CO, H/sub 2/O mixture.",
